  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Finely shred the cabbage. Trim the snow peas, then halve on an angle. Coarsely chop three-quarters of the cashews (see Kitchen note). Crush or finely chop 1 garlic clove. Drain and rinse the mixed beans.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/141954/photos/large/prep_ingredients-af9b78214c3361ddb23c4e9971339b81.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Start cooking beans: Heat 2 tsp olive oil in a medium deep frypan over medium heat. Cook the mixed beans, garlic and 2 tsp Indian masala seasoning, stirring, for 1 min or until fragrant.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/141955/photos/large/start_cooking_beans-f7f229c05a27a799e685060045b5dde2.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Simmer beans: Add the coconut milk and 80ml (⅓ cup) water, season with salt and pepper and bring to a simmer. Cook, stirring occasionally, for 10 mins or until the sauce is slightly reduced. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/141956/photos/large/simmer_beans-0bfb37db621a29216dd42691383a47cf.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prep veggies: Meanwhile, bring a small saucepan of water to the boil for the snow peas. Combine 2 tsp white vinegar and ½ tsp honey in a large bowl. Add the cabbage, season with salt and pepper and toss to combine. Cook the snow peas in the pan of boiling water for 1 min or until bright green. Drain and season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/141957/photos/large/prep_veggies-ca2db4847800409f042672a2f745835c.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the masala beans, cabbage and snow peas among bowls. Scatter over the cashews and enjoy.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/141958/photos/large/serve_up-95fbd95c0a9f5292526e583ea878717d.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen note: To keep within our healthy eating guidelines, we've used only three-quarters of the cashews.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/141959/photos/large/make_it_yours-506b629beebe801a18634f88df01d1b1.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
